IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgia-interpretation-time`

-- Interpretation Act 1965 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from
-- 5 December 2025 -- LAYER 1, PART 6: MISCELLANEOUS, ss 42 to 49, 54 and 55.
-- (ss 50 to 53, on time, are in sgia-interpretation-time.l4.)
-- Policy for "in the absence of any provision to the contrary" / "unless the contrary intention appears":
-- a plain yes/no input, NOTHING when it is TRUE.

§ `Section 42 -- powers of President, Minister or other authority to appoint public officer to serve on board`

-- src:1924 | 42.—(1) Where under the provisions of any Act power is given to
-- src:1925 | the President, a Minister or any other authority to appoint any person
-- src:1926 | to be a member of any board, commission, committee or similar body,
-- src:1927 | it is lawful for the President, Minister or other authority, in the
-- src:1928 | absence of any provision to the contrary, to appoint, by his or her
-- src:1929 | official designation, any public officer.
@ref s 42(1) (src:1924-1929)
GIVEN `power is given by an Act to appoint a person to be a member of a board, commission, committee or similar body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person to be appointed is a public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment is by his or her official designation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision to the contrary appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is lawful to appoint the public officer by his or her official designation` `power is given by an Act to appoint a person to be a member of a board, commission, committee or similar body` `the person to be appointed is a public officer` `the appointment is by his or her official designation` `a provision to the contrary appears` MEANS
    IF `power is given by an Act to appoint a person to be a member of a board, commission, committee or similar body`
       AND `the person to be appointed is a public officer`
       AND `the appointment is by his or her official designation`
       AND (NOT `a provision to the contrary appears`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1934 | (2) On such appointment and until the appointment is cancelled or
-- src:1935 | otherwise determined, the person for the time being holding or
-- src:1936 | carrying out the duties of the office in question is a member of that
-- src:1937 | board, commission, committee or similar body.
@ref s 42(2) (src:1934-1937)
GIVEN `a public officer has been appointed to the board by official designation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment has been cancelled or otherwise determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person for the time being holding or carrying out the duties of the office is a member of the board` `a public officer has been appointed to the board by official designation` `the appointment has been cancelled or otherwise determined` MEANS
    IF `a public officer has been appointed to the board by official designation` AND (NOT `the appointment has been cancelled or otherwise determined`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1939 | (3) Where under the provisions of any Act power is given to the
-- src:1940 | President, a Minister or any other authority to appoint any board,
-- src:1941 | commission, committee or similar body, it is lawful for the President,
-- src:1942 | Minister or other authority, in the absence of any provision to the
-- src:1943 | contrary, to appoint a chairperson of that board, commission,
-- src:1944 | committee or similar body.
@ref s 42(3) (src:1939-1944)
GIVEN `power is given by an Act to appoint a board, commission, committee or similar body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a provision to the contrary appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is lawful to appoint a chairperson of the body` `power is given by an Act to appoint a board, commission, committee or similar body` `a provision to the contrary appears` MEANS
    IF `power is given by an Act to appoint a board, commission, committee or similar body` AND (NOT `a provision to the contrary appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Sections 43 and 44 -- prima facie evidence of signature; public officers`

-- src:1948 | 43. Where the fiat, authorisation or sanction of the President, a
-- src:1949 | Minister, the Attorney‑General, a Deputy Attorney‑General, the
-- src:1950 | Solicitor‑General, the Public Prosecutor, a Deputy Public Prosecutor
-- src:1951 | or any public officer is necessary before any prosecution or action is
-- src:1952 | commenced or for any purpose in connection with any proceeding,
-- src:1953 | any document purporting to bear the fiat, authorisation or sanction of
-- src:1954 | the President, Minister, Attorney‑General, Deputy Attorney‑General,
-- src:1955 | Solicitor‑General, Public Prosecutor, Deputy Public Prosecutor or
-- src:1956 | public officer (as the case may be) is to be received as prima facie
-- src:1957 | evidence in any proceeding without proof being given that the
-- src:1958 | signature to such fiat, authorisation or sanction is that of the
-- src:1959 | President, Minister, Attorney‑General, Deputy Attorney‑General,
-- src:1960 | Solicitor‑General, Public Prosecutor, Deputy Public Prosecutor or
-- src:1961 | public officer, as the case may be.
@ref s 43 (src:1948-1961)
GIVEN `the fiat, authorisation or sanction of the President, a Minister, the Attorney-General, a Deputy Attorney-General, the Solicitor-General, the Public Prosecutor, a Deputy Public Prosecutor or a public officer is necessary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document purports to bear the fiat, authorisation or sanction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the document is received as prima facie evidence without proof that the signature is that of the officer` `the fiat, authorisation or sanction of the President, a Minister, the Attorney-General, a Deputy Attorney-General, the Solicitor-General, the Public Prosecutor, a Deputy Public Prosecutor or a public officer is necessary` `the document purports to bear the fiat, authorisation or sanction` MEANS
    IF `the fiat, authorisation or sanction of the President, a Minister, the Attorney-General, a Deputy Attorney-General, the Solicitor-General, the Public Prosecutor, a Deputy Public Prosecutor or a public officer is necessary` AND `the document purports to bear the fiat, authorisation or sanction`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:1967 | 44. A reference in any written law to any public officer by the usual
-- src:1968 | or common title of his or her office is, if there is such an office
-- src:1969 | customarily in Singapore and unless the contrary intention appears, to
-- src:1970 | be read and construed as referring to the person for the time being
-- src:1971 | holding or carrying out the duties of that office in Singapore.
@ref s 44 (src:1967-1971)
GIVEN `the reference is to a public officer by the usual or common title of his or her office` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is such an office customarily in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the reference is read as referring to the person for the time being holding or carrying out the duties of that office in Singapore` `the reference is to a public officer by the usual or common title of his or her office` `there is such an office customarily in Singapore` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `the reference is to a public officer by the usual or common title of his or her office` AND `there is such an office customarily in Singapore` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 45 -- an act for which payment is required need not be performed until payment is made`

-- src:1979 | 45.—(1) Where any person, public officer, public department or
-- src:1980 | statutory authority is required to do anything for which a fee is to be
-- src:1981 | paid or a charge made under any written law, the person, public
-- src:1982 | officer, public department or statutory authority may decline to do
-- src:1983 | that thing —
-- src:1985 | (a) until the fee is paid or payment is made; and
-- src:1987 | (b) where the precise amount of the payment to be made
-- src:1988 | cannot be ascertained until the thing is done, until there is
-- src:1989 | paid an amount that may be estimated to be the correct
-- src:1990 | amount by the person, public officer, public department or
-- src:1991 | statutory authority required to do that thing.
@ref s 45(1) (src:1979-1991)
GIVEN `a person, public officer, public department or statutory authority is required to do something for which a fee is to be paid or a charge made under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the precise amount of the payment cannot be ascertained until the thing is done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the fee or charge has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an amount estimated to be the correct amount has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the person, officer, department or authority may decline to do the thing` `a person, public officer, public department or statutory authority is required to do something for which a fee is to be paid or a charge made under a written law` `the precise amount of the payment cannot be ascertained until the thing is done` `the fee or charge has been paid` `an amount estimated to be the correct amount has been paid` MEANS
    IF `a person, public officer, public department or statutory authority is required to do something for which a fee is to be paid or a charge made under a written law`
    THEN JUST (NOT (IF `the precise amount of the payment cannot be ascertained until the thing is done`
                    THEN `an amount estimated to be the correct amount has been paid`
                    ELSE `the fee or charge has been paid`))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- A positive result is a further payment owed; a negative result is a refund due; zero is nothing to adjust.
-- src:1993 | (2) Where a thing has been done for which an estimated amount has
-- src:1994 | been paid, the amount must be adjusted to the correct amount either
-- src:1995 | by means of a further payment or by a refund of the amount overpaid.
@ref s 45(2) (src:1993-1995)
GIVEN `the estimated amount paid` IS A NUMBER
      `the correct amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the adjustment after the thing has been done` `the estimated amount paid` `the correct amount` MEANS
    `the correct amount` MINUS `the estimated amount paid`

§ `Section 46 -- fees or charges may be prescribed and may be reduced, varied, remitted or refunded`

-- src:2000 | 46.—(1) Where any act is required to be done or a service
-- src:2001 | performed by a public body, statutory authority or public officer
-- src:2002 | under or in connection with any written law, and no special provision
-- src:2003 | is made thereby or thereunder for making a charge in respect of the
-- src:2004 | act or service, the Minister may, by order published in the Gazette,
-- src:2005 | provide for the imposition of —
-- src:2007 | (a) such fees or charges as he may consider proper;
-- src:2009 | (b) the charges and penalties for the late payment of any fee or
-- src:2010 | charge referred to in paragraph (a); and
-- src:2012 | (c) the interest payable on any outstanding amount of any fee,
-- src:2013 | charge or penalty referred to in paragraph (a) or (b) or for
-- src:2014 | any payment thereof by instalment.
@ref s 46(1) (src:2000-2014)
GIVEN `an act is required to be done or a service performed by a public body, statutory authority or public officer under or in connection with a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `special provision is made for a charge in respect of the act or service` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Minister may by order published in the Gazette provide for fees or charges, charges and penalties for late payment, and interest` `an act is required to be done or a service performed by a public body, statutory authority or public officer under or in connection with a written law` `special provision is made for a charge in respect of the act or service` MEANS
    IF `an act is required to be done or a service performed by a public body, statutory authority or public officer under or in connection with a written law` AND (NOT `special provision is made for a charge in respect of the act or service`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2016 | (2) Any fee or charge, any charge or penalty for the late payment of
-- src:2017 | any fee or charge, and any interest payable on any outstanding
-- src:2018 | amount of any fee, charge or penalty or for any payment thereof by
-- src:2019 | instalment, under any written law made payable to the Government or
-- src:2024 | to any public body, statutory authority or public officer (not being any
-- src:2025 | fee, charge, penalty or interest which is regulated by Rules of Court)
-- src:2026 | may by order of the Minister be reduced, remitted or refunded, in
-- src:2027 | whole or in part in the circumstances of any particular case.
@ref s 46(2) (src:2016-2027)
GIVEN `it is a fee, charge, penalty or interest made payable under a written law to the Government or a public body, statutory authority or public officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is regulated by Rules of Court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Minister may by order reduce, remit or refund it in whole or in part in the circumstances of a particular case` `it is a fee, charge, penalty or interest made payable under a written law to the Government or a public body, statutory authority or public officer` `it is regulated by Rules of Court` MEANS
    IF `it is a fee, charge, penalty or interest made payable under a written law to the Government or a public body, statutory authority or public officer` AND (NOT `it is regulated by Rules of Court`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 47 -- proceedings not to abate on death, etc., of official`

-- src:2033 | 47. Any civil or criminal proceedings taken by or against any
-- src:2034 | person by virtue of his or her office are not discontinued or abated by
-- src:2035 | his or her death, resignation, absence or removal from office, but may
-- src:2036 | be carried on by or against (as the case may be) the person appointed
-- src:2037 | to perform the duties of the office.
@ref s 47 (src:2033-2037)
GIVEN `the proceedings are civil or criminal and are taken by or against a person by virtue of his or her office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the proceedings are discontinued or abated by the death, resignation, absence or removal from office` `the proceedings are civil or criminal and are taken by or against a person by virtue of his or her office` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are civil or criminal and are taken by or against a person by virtue of his or her office` THEN JUST FALSE ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 47 but may be carried on by or against the person appointed to perform the duties of the office (src:2035-2037)
GIVEN `the proceedings are civil or criminal and are taken by or against a person by virtue of his or her office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the proceedings may be carried on by or against the person appointed to perform the duties of the office` `the proceedings are civil or criminal and are taken by or against a person by virtue of his or her office` MEANS
    IF `the proceedings are civil or criminal and are taken by or against a person by virtue of his or her office` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 48 -- the Gazette`

DECLARE `Form of the Gazette` IS ONE OF
    `the prescribed website`
    `print`
    `another electronic form`
    `another prescribed form`

-- src:2041 | 48.—(1) The Gazette is to be published by the authority of any
-- src:2042 | written law or of the Government.
-- src:2044 | (2) The Gazette may be published in one or more forms, including
-- src:2045 | on the prescribed website, in any other electronic form and in print.
@ref s 48(1), (2) (src:2041-2045)
GIVEN `the Gazette is published by the authority of a written law or of the Government` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form` IS A `Form of the Gazette`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Gazette may be published in this form` `the Gazette is published by the authority of a written law or of the Government` `the form` MEANS
    IF `the Gazette is published by the authority of a written law or of the Government`
    THEN CONSIDER `the form`
         WHEN `the prescribed website` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `print` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `another electronic form` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `another prescribed form` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 48(3): a Gazette published in 2 or more forms is deemed published on the date it is first published in any form.
-- src:2047 | (3) If a Gazette is published in 2 or more forms, that Gazette is
-- src:2048 | deemed to be published on the date on which that Gazette is first
-- src:2049 | published in any form.
@ref s 48(3) (src:2047-2049)
GIVEN `the dates the Gazette was published in each form` IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`the date a Gazette published in 2 or more forms is deemed published` `the dates the Gazette was published in each form` MEANS
    IF count `the dates the Gazette was published in each form` AT LEAST 2
    THEN JUST (Date (minimum (map (GIVEN d YIELD Day d) `the dates the Gazette was published in each form`)))
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2051 | (4) The Gazette published in each of the following forms is to be
-- src:2052 | judicially noticed:
-- src:2054 | (a) the Gazette published on the prescribed website on or after
-- src:2055 | the appointed date;
-- src:2057 | (b) the Gazette published in print;
-- src:2059 | (c) any other form of the Gazette that is prescribed,
-- src:2061 | and, for the purpose of paragraph (b), reference may be made to any
-- src:2062 | printed document purporting to be the Gazette published by authority
-- src:2063 | and printed by the Government Printer.
@ref s 48(4) (src:2051-2063)
GIVEN `the form` IS A `Form of the Gazette`
      `the prescribed website Gazette was published on or after the appointed date` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other form is prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the Gazette in this form is to be judicially noticed` `the form` `the prescribed website Gazette was published on or after the appointed date` `the other form is prescribed` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form`
    WHEN `the prescribed website` THEN JUST `the prescribed website Gazette was published on or after the appointed date`
    WHEN `print` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `another prescribed form` THEN JUST `the other form is prescribed`
    WHEN `another electronic form` THEN NOTHING

-- src:2065 | (5) Subject to subsections (6) and (7), the Gazette published in each
-- src:2066 | of the forms mentioned in subsection (4) is, in all courts and for all
-- src:2067 | purposes, prima facie evidence of the matters published therein.
@ref s 48(5) (src:2065-2067)
GIVEN `the Gazette is judicially noticed in this form under section 48(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`it is, in all courts and for all purposes, prima facie evidence of the matters published in it` `the Gazette is judicially noticed in this form under section 48(4)` MEANS
    IF `the Gazette is judicially noticed in this form under section 48(4)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- s 48(6), (7): which form prevails over another, to the extent of any inconsistency, depends on whether the
-- publication was on or after the "appointed date" (the date section 2 of the Electronic Gazette and Legislation
-- Act 2025 commences, a fact the Act borrows from that Act; asked as an input).
-- The answer is for `the form` against `the other form`: JUST TRUE when the Act says it prevails, JUST FALSE when
-- the Act says the other form prevails over it, and NOTHING for every pair the Act does not speak to
--   (6) on or after the appointed date: the prescribed website prevails over the Gazette in any other form;
--   (7) before the appointed date: print prevails over the Gazette in any other form;
-- so, for example, print against another electronic form after the appointed date is NOTHING.
-- src:2072 | (6) To the extent of any inconsistency, a Gazette published on the
-- src:2073 | prescribed website on or after the appointed date prevails over that
-- src:2074 | Gazette published in any other form on or after that date.
-- src:2076 | (7) To the extent of any inconsistency, a Gazette published in print
-- src:2077 | before the appointed date prevails over that Gazette published in any
-- src:2078 | other form before that date.
-- src:2087 | (9) In this section, “appointed date” means the date of
-- src:2088 | commencement of section 2 of the Electronic Gazette and
-- src:2089 | Legislation Act 2025.
@ref s 48(6), (7), (9) (src:2072-2089)
GIVEN `the form` IS A `Form of the Gazette`
      `the other form` IS A `Form of the Gazette`
      `the day of publication` IS A DATE
      `the appointed date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`this form prevails over the other form to the extent of any inconsistency` `the form` `the other form` `the day of publication` `the appointed date` MEANS
    IF `the day of publication` AT LEAST `the appointed date`
    THEN BRANCH
             IF `the form` EQUALS `the prescribed website` AND (NOT (`the other form` EQUALS `the prescribed website`)) THEN JUST TRUE
             IF `the other form` EQUALS `the prescribed website` AND (NOT (`the form` EQUALS `the prescribed website`)) THEN JUST FALSE
             OTHERWISE NOTHING
    ELSE BRANCH
             IF `the form` EQUALS `print` AND (NOT (`the other form` EQUALS `print`)) THEN JUST TRUE
             IF `the other form` EQUALS `print` AND (NOT (`the form` EQUALS `print`)) THEN JUST FALSE
             OTHERWISE NOTHING

§ `Section 48A -- service of documents`

DECLARE `Whom a document is served on` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a partnership`
    `a body corporate`

DECLARE `How a document is served` IS ONE OF
    `by delivering it to the individual personally`
    `by leaving it at the usual or last known address of the place of residence or business of the individual`
    `by sending it by prepaid post to the usual or last known address of the place of residence or business of the individual`
    `by delivering it to the secretary or other like officer of the partnership`
    `by leaving it at the principal or last known place of business of the partnership in Singapore`
    `by sending it by prepaid post to the principal or last known place of business of the partnership in Singapore`
    `by delivering it to the secretary or other like officer of the body corporate`
    `by leaving it at the registered office or a principal office of the body corporate in Singapore`
    `by sending it by prepaid post to the registered office or a principal office of the body corporate in Singapore`
    `in some other way`

-- src:2095 | 48A.—(1) Where a written law authorises or requires a document
-- src:2096 | to be served on a person, whether the expression “serve”, “give” or
-- src:2097 | “send” or any other expression is used, then, unless the contrary
-- src:2098 | intention appears, the document may be served —
-- src:2100 | (a) in the case of an individual —
-- src:2102 | (i) by delivering it to the individual personally; or
-- src:2104 | (ii) by leaving it at, or by sending it by prepaid post to,
-- src:2105 | the usual or last known address of the place of
-- src:2106 | residence or business of the individual;
-- src:2108 | (b) in the case of a partnership —
-- src:2110 | (i) by delivering it to the secretary or other like officer
-- src:2111 | of the partnership; or
-- src:2113 | (ii) by leaving it at, or by sending it by prepaid post to,
-- src:2114 | the principal or last known place of business of the
-- src:2115 | partnership in Singapore;
-- src:2120 | (c) in the case of a body corporate —
-- src:2122 | (i) by delivering it to the secretary or other like officer
-- src:2123 | of the body corporate; or
-- src:2125 | (ii) by leaving it at, or by sending it by prepaid post to,
-- src:2126 | the registered office or a principal office of the body
-- src:2127 | corporate in Singapore.
@ref s 48A(1) (src:2095-2127)
GIVEN `a written law authorises or requires a document to be served on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `whom` IS A `Whom a document is served on`
      `how` IS A `How a document is served`
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the document may be served this way` `a written law authorises or requires a document to be served on a person` `whom` `how` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a written law authorises or requires a document to be served on a person` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`)
    THEN CONSIDER `whom`
         WHEN `an individual` THEN
             CONSIDER `how`
             WHEN `by delivering it to the individual personally` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `by leaving it at the usual or last known address of the place of residence or business of the individual` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `by sending it by prepaid post to the usual or last known address of the place of residence or business of the individual` THEN JUST TRUE
             OTHERWISE NOTHING
         WHEN `a partnership` THEN
             CONSIDER `how`
             WHEN `by delivering it to the secretary or other like officer of the partnership` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `by leaving it at the principal or last known place of business of the partnership in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `by sending it by prepaid post to the principal or last known place of business of the partnership in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
             OTHERWISE NOTHING
         WHEN `a body corporate` THEN
             CONSIDER `how`
             WHEN `by delivering it to the secretary or other like officer of the body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `by leaving it at the registered office or a principal office of the body corporate in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
             WHEN `by sending it by prepaid post to the registered office or a principal office of the body corporate in Singapore` THEN JUST TRUE
             OTHERWISE NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2129 | (2) Nothing in subsection (1) —
-- src:2131 | (a) affects the operation of any written law that authorises the
-- src:2132 | service of a document otherwise than as provided in that
-- src:2133 | subsection; or
-- src:2135 | (b) affects the power of a court to authorise service of a
-- src:2136 | document otherwise than as provided in that subsection.
@ref s 48A(2) (src:2129-2136)
GIVEN `another written law authorises service otherwise, or a court has authorised service otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 48A(1) affects that other way of serving` `another written law authorises service otherwise, or a court has authorised service otherwise` MEANS
    FALSE

§ `Sections 49, 54 and 55`

-- src:2140 | 49. In the measurement of any distance for the purposes of any
-- src:2141 | written law, that distance must, unless the contrary intention appears,
-- src:2142 | be measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane.
@ref s 49 (src:2140-2142)
GIVEN `a distance is measured for the purposes of a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the distance is measured in a straight line on a horizontal plane` `a distance is measured for the purposes of a written law` `a contrary intention appears` MEANS
    IF `a distance is measured for the purposes of a written law` AND (NOT `a contrary intention appears`) THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:2203 | 54. No Act affects in any manner the rights of the Government
-- src:2204 | unless it is therein expressly provided, or unless it appears by
-- src:2205 | necessary implication, that the Government is bound thereby.
@ref s 54 (src:2203-2205)
GIVEN `the Act expressly provides that the Government is bound` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears by necessary implication that the Government is bound` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Act affects the rights of the Government` `the Act expressly provides that the Government is bound` `it appears by necessary implication that the Government is bound` MEANS
    `the Act expressly provides that the Government is bound` OR `it appears by necessary implication that the Government is bound`

-- src:2208 | 55. This Act binds the Government.
@ref s 55 (src:2208-2208)
`this Act binds the Government` MEANS TRUE
